d egocentric attitude are concerns but perhaps less severe. Emily may decide to switch to C. She should state that.\n\nThus Emily's public message: Acknowledge James and Sarah's points, note B's memory and hostile remarks, which are critical, and that C's reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh his communication issues. She may still note that C's egocentric and unwillingness to further education are concerns but can be mitigated. She will now vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\". Ensure format: {\"agent\": \"emily_brooks\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}.\n\nProceed."}
