illing to further education) and suggest mitigation. Or we could bring up Candidate D as a possible alternative, but we haven't discussed D much. However we still need to cover all candidates before final recommendation. The shared mental model says Candidate D is still under-discussed. We could use this turn to bring up D, but we need to keep it focused. The instruction says we should still cover all candidates before final recommendation. So we could introduce D now, but we need to tie it to the current discussion. Perhaps we can say: \"While I agree with Emily that C is currently strongest, we still need to consider D, whose strengths include problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but concerns about arrogance and weak leadership.\" That would bring D into discussion. Then we can state our recommendation remains C, but we need to discuss D further. That would satisfy coverage.\n\nThus Sarah's public message: Agree with Emily, note that C's strengths outweigh concerns, but we still need to evaluate D's profile before final decision. Vote remains Candidate C.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
